# **6. Lessons Learned**
- SMB shares often leak sensitive credentials when misconfigured.  
- Windows registry keys can expose stored auto‑logon passwords.  
- Writable service binaries remain one of the most reliable Windows privilege escalation vectors.  
- Scheduled tasks running as SYSTEM are extremely dangerous when their associated files are modifiable.  
- Lateral movement in Windows often relies on chaining small misconfigurations rather than a single explooit.

